      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The role of psychic factors in the most common somatic diseases (chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, bronchial asthma, peptic ulcer, h4epatitis, rheumatoid arthritis, systemic lupus erythematosus, cancer, and chronic renal failure) is considered in Part II of the review. A significant connection between anxiety and depression and the occurrence, course, and prognosis of many diseases is shown. The appropriateness and effectiveness of treatment of mental disorders is evaluated on the basis of randomized studies."},
